Due to our thorough reform of the judicial system, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> behind these documents can now be publicly exposed and prosecuted by the state for high treason. This has dealt a severe blow to the constitutional appearance of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, causing great distrust between them and the bourgeois establishment, including President DuFour himself.

Our Hesse government is set to continue in a caretaker capacity for the foreseeable future, following the collapse of talks between the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> and [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].

@nothing
view-if: judicial_reform < 4
on-arrival: boxheim_persecuted = 0; knight_dissent -= 10; knight_strength += 5; commons_royalist -= 2; burgher_royalist -= 6; guild_royalist -= 6; landed_royalist -= 2; pro_republic += 5; loyalist_militancy -= 0.05; commons_marcher += 2; burgher_marcher += 2

Expectedly, the Ministry of Justice believes that the documents did not constitute a crime of high treason, as they argue that the document was directed against <span style="color: #700000;">communist</span> putschists, rather than the government. [? if bruning_time: We are sure that Chancellor Askew is behind this downplaying, to keep cooperation with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> open. ?]

We have at least discredited the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> in the eyes of many, and have managed to keep our Hesse government functioning in a caretaker capacity due to the collapse of talks between the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> and [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].